---
layout: null
---
{% comment %}
  Machine-readable copy of the track list, served at chappie.online/tracks.json
  for the mod's Tracks tab to fetch.

  This exists because Jekyll consumes _data/tracks.yml at build time and never
  serves it — there is no URL for the raw file. Generating from the same data
  means the page a human reads and the endpoint the mod reads can never
  disagree; adding a track to _data/tracks.yml updates both.

  layout: null keeps the site's HTML wrapper off it. _config.yml applies the
  default layout to every path, so this has to opt out explicitly or the JSON
  arrives wrapped in a full page.
{% endcomment %}
{"generated":"{{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema }}","tracks":{{ site.data.tracks.tracks | default: empty | jsonify }}}
